# Security headers for Cloudflare Workers static assets. Hugo copies this file
# verbatim from static/ to public/, which is the assets directory wrangler
# uploads (see wrangler.jsonc). Keep in sync with netlify.toml, which declares
# the same headers for the alternative host.
#
# Cloudflare applies every matching rule in file order. Repeating a header name
# across two matching rules joins the values with a comma, so the /games/*
# override below first detaches X-Frame-Options ("! " prefix) and then re-sets
# it — otherwise it would come out as "DENY, SAMEORIGIN".

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Asteroids is embedded same-origin in the project case study
# (content/projects/asteroids.md), so framing must be allowed here.
/games/*
  ! X-Frame-Options
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
